{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.ChainBindingNoSaturationPeak","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ChainBindingNoSaturationPeak","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.chain_no_saturation_peak","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.chain_no_saturation_peak","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChainBindingNoSaturationPeak.lean#L117-L130","doc":"**No saturation peak.** For any per-bond constants, any `α`, and any isospin\nexcess, the per-nucleon chain binding does not exceed both of its neighbours at\nan interior mass number — so it cannot reproduce the measured interior maximum of\n`B/A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.chainPerNucleon_eq_hyperbola","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.chainPerNucleon_eq_hyperbola","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChainBindingNoSaturationPeak.lean#L105-L115","doc":"**The exact hyperbolic identity.** Along any isobaric chain the per-nucleon\nchain binding is exactly `c₁ + c₂/A`, with the asymptote `c₁ = α(L_pp+L_nn)/2`\n**independent of the isospin excess `d`** — all of the `d`-dependence sits in the\n`1/A` coefficient. An identity, discharged by `ring`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.chainPerNucleon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.chainPerNucleon","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChainBindingNoSaturationPeak.lean#L98-L103","doc":"Per-nucleon linear-chain binding along the isobaric chain of isospin excess\n`d = N − Z`, i.e. with `Z = (A−d)/2` and `N = (A+d)/2`:\n\n    B_sym/A = α·[ (Z−1)L_pp + L_pn + (N−1)L_nn ] / A. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.hyperbola_no_interior_max","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.hyperbola_no_interior_max","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ChainBindingNoSaturationPeak.lean#L82-L96","doc":"**The monotonicity invariant.** A hyperbola `A ↦ c₁ + c₂/A` on `A > 0` never\ntakes a value at an interior point `b` strictly greater than at *both* of\n`a < b < c`. It is monotone, so it has no strict interior maximum.\n\nProof: the two hypotheses force `c₂ < 0` and `c₂ > 0` respectively. ","signatureChunk":0}]}